          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मौन (maun) is a tatsama, borrowed from Sanskrit mauna, \"silence, taciturnity\", from muni, \"a silent sage\" (Monier-Williams). It is the formal, chosen silence; cup is the everyday kind."
            }
          ]
